# .cursorrules — mirror of CLAUDE.md (see that file for the full version)

This is a local-first, installable PWA (React + Vite) that teaches AI from a fixed
curriculum. Lessons are generated by an LLM using the user's own API key and
cached on-device in IndexedDB. No backend. Deploys on GitHub Pages.

Rules:
- Explain each file's purpose in inline comments — the reader is a beginner.
- Prefer simple, readable code over clever one-liners.
- After each function/file, note edge cases it does NOT handle.
- Don't add a library without justifying why it's worth it.
- On errors, diagnose the root cause before fixing.

Must-not-regress behavior:
- API key stored only in localStorage, sent only to the LLM provider; show the
  low-spending-cap warning; public visitors enter their own key.
- Lessons are cached after first generation; only "Regenerate" re-spends tokens.
- Lessons use the premium model; flashcards/quizzes use the cheap model.
- All data is exportable/importable as JSON.
